    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=## Your Task\n\nDo a wide research on this B2B SaaS company and return every interesting link that shows what they do, who they sell to, and any proof they have. The focus is sales assets — anything that shows results, demonstrates the product, or builds credibility with a buyer.\n\nNo analysis. No summaries. Links only, each with a one-line factual description\n\nCompany Name: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Name }}\nWebsite: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Website }}\n\n(NOTICE the WEBSITE do you are not confusing the company with other companies. DO NOT get mixed by signs. RESEARCH ONLY the the company from the website above)\n\nIf nothing is found for a section, write: None found.\n\n---\n\n# OUTPUT FORMAT\n\n---\n\n## 1. Sales Assets (PRIMARY FOCUS)\n\nFind every piece of content that could serve as proof or pre-sell material. Cast wide — check the website, YouTube, LinkedIn, podcast platforms, media sites, and anywhere else.\n\n- Case studies (link each individually — include the customer name and result if visible in the title or URL)\n- Customer testimonials or results pages\n- VSL or founder explainer video (YouTube, Loom, Wistia, or embedded on site)\n- Product demo video (recorded walkthrough)\n- Results screenshots or data pages\n- Any video content about the product — interviews, walkthroughs, explainers, webinars\n- G2, Capterra, or Trustpilot review pages\n- Linkedin Posts or featured stuff from their decision makres Linkedins\n\nFormat: URL - one-line description (note what proof or result is shown if visible)\n\n---\n\n## 2. External Mentions\n\n- Funding announcements (TechCrunch, Crunchbase, Israeli tech press, Geektime)\n- Podcast appearances (founder interviews, SaaS or sales podcasts)\n- Conference talks or speaker pages\n- Product Hunt launch page\n- Any notable press or community coverage\n- Reddit or community threads mentioning the product\n\nFormat: URL - one-line description\n\n---\n\n## 3. Sales-Led Signals (SECONDARY)\n\nOnly include if found easily — do not spend significant time here:\n\n- Job postings for AE, SDR, BDR, VP Sales roles (LinkedIn Jobs or careers page)\n- Enterprise pricing tier page (SSO, RBAC, procurement support visible)\n\nFormat: URL - one-line description\n\n---\n\n# RULES\n\n1. Links only. No analysis, no interpretation, no strategy.\n2. Every link must include a one-line factual description.\n3. Section 1 is the priority. Find every sales asset that exists before moving to other sections.\n4. Do not include social profiles, Meta Ads Library, or standard website pages — these are already captured elsewhere.\n5. If something is not found, write: None found. Never invent a URL.\n",
        "options": {}
      },
